/-!
# Enumeration of the second nonsplit centralizer candidate

The 384 rows are explicit permutations, each accompanied by a positive word
in the two published generators. Checked transitions under the generators and
their inverses prove that these rows exhaust the exact generated subgroup.
A tuple of point images distinguishes the rows. Thus the resulting enumeration
is a bijection to `NonsplitModels.Second`, with its inherited group law.

The tables were generated by breadth-first multiplication of the published
permutations; every equation used here is checked by the Lean kernel. This
certifies the carrier and its order, not its exclusion as an involution
centralizer. Source problem: Huppert--Blackburn III, XII.1.18(b), p.314.
-/

